// games/sonic4/data/effects/ojz_scenes.emp — the AUTHORED scenes (spec 2026-08-17 §2/§3).
//
// The twenty shipped parallax configurations, re-authored in the scene model: world-Y
// layers plus attachments, with the lowering to parallax_config/band_entry owned by
// engine/level/scene_dsl.emp and the emission owned by data/effects/scene_registry.emp.
// This module holds NO record shapes and NO hdr()/band() calls — that is the point.
//
// THE SWAP LANDED (Task 9). games/sonic4/data/parallax/configs.emp is DELETED; the six
// tables and the twenty records carry their shipped names, and this module plus
// data/effects/scene_registry.emp are the only authoring surface for either. The
// temporary `SceneOut_` prefixes that let both record sets link at once during Tasks 6-8
// are gone with the file that made them necessary.
//
// GLOB IMPORTS ARE MANDATORY (both of them). A comptime fn's free names resolve at the
// CALL SITE, and engine.level.scene_dsl is NOT a member of sigil's COMPTIME_HELPERS set
// (crates/sigil-harness/src/native.rs:1942 — parallax_dsl IS, scene_dsl is not), so
// nothing it defines is ambient. A selective `use ...{scene, layer}` is loud on the
// function axis and SILENT on the constant axis. See the pin block at the top of
// engine/level/scene_dsl.emp for the whole rule.
//
// EVERY VALUE BELOW IS TRANSCRIBED FROM games/sonic4/data/parallax/configs.emp, with the
// cited line number beside each scene. configs.emp's `cell: N` was a Plane-B cell row.
//
// ---- THE UNIT CHANGED TWICE, AND THE SECOND TIME IS P3 TASK 7 (world-Y re-glue) ----
//
// P1: `world_y = cell * 8`, i.e. PLANE-B PIXELS, and scene_band() reversed it with `>> 3`.
// P3: `world_y` is an ACT world Y, and `scene_plane_line()` maps it to a plane LINE with
//     the scene's own vertical mapping — the same one Parallax_Step5_Vscroll applies to
//     the camera, `((world_y - v_center) >> v_factor) + v_offset`.
//
// FOR THE EIGHTEEN LOCKED SCENES (`v_factor: 15`) NOTHING MOVED. A locked BG plane
// ignores the camera, so the mapping is the identity and their tops (0/32/80/112/160)
// are the same numbers meaning the same rows.
//
// FOR THE TWO UNLOCKED OJZ SCENES the numbers changed and the BANDS DID NOT. OJZ_Default
// and OJZ_Underwater run `v_factor 3 / v_center 512 / v_offset 0`, so plane line
// `(W - 512) >> 3` and the four shipped plane lines 0 / 64 / 320 / 384 are the images of
// act Y 512 / 1024 / 3072 / 3584. Those are the values authored below. Read them as: the
// bands sit at act heights 512..3584 in a 6144-px-tall act, and the BG art shows them
// eight times compressed, which is what `v_factor 3` means.
//
// The old plane-space numbers are recoverable from any of these by the mapping above;
// they are NOT recoverable by reading the authored value, which is the entire point of
// the change — a plane coordinate said nothing about where in the act the horizon was.
//
// THE FAMILY HELPERS BELOW ARE `pub` FOR A MECHANICAL REASON, not for reuse: a `use` edge
// re-evaluates an imported const's initializer in the CONSUMER's scope (Task 5's probe
// finding, recorded in scene_registry.emp's banner), so scene_registry's glob import of
// this module re-runs `haze_scene(speed: 1)` there. A private helper would report
// `unknown function haze_scene` at a span inside THIS file. Same reason every helper in
// scene_dsl.emp is `pub`.
//
// PURE COMPTIME — this module emits ZERO bytes. Both the twenty records and the six
// deform tables they attach are emitted by data/effects/scene_registry.emp, the sole
// emission path (see the import note below for why the tables live there and not here).
module games.sonic4.ojz_scenes in ojz_scenes

use engine.level.scene_dsl.*
use engine.level.parallax_dsl.*
// THE SIX DEFORM TABLES ARE EMITTED BY THE REGISTRY, AND THAT IS A ROM-LAYOUT FACT, not a
// preference. The shipped record block INTERLEAVES tables and records (DeformTable_Zero,
// OJZ_Default, OJZ_Underwater, DeformTable_OJZ_Calm, OJZ_Windy, ...), and a section is
// contiguous per module, so tables emitted from HERE would land as one 1536-byte run ahead
// of the records — same bytes, different addresses, and therefore different
// `pcfg_deform_table_*` pointers inside every record. That is the whole image-identity gate
// (spec §8.1). The tables are declared in scene_registry.emp in the shipped order and
// imported back here as Labels; their VALUES are the `SceneSrc_*` consts below, which stay
// with the scenes that attach them.
//
// The import must be a name list, and it is not a const import: these are `pub data`
// LABELS. (The Task-5 clone-injection trap is a CONST-axis trap — an imported const's
// initializer re-evaluates in the consumer's scope. A label import is a symbol reference.)
use games.sonic4.scene_registry.{DeformTable_Zero, DeformTable_OJZ_Calm, DeformTable_Shimmer,
                                 DeformTable_Haze, DeformTable_Rocking, DeformTable_Perspective,
                                 RowRemapLadder_Waterline16}

// =====================================================================
// The six deformation tables, verbatim from configs.emp — same generators, same
// arguments, same 256 signed bytes. These are DATA, not authored model: a scene attaches
// one through SceneDeform / SceneVDeform and never looks inside it.
//
//   DeformTable_Zero         deform_zero()
//   DeformTable_OJZ_Calm     deform_sine(amplitude: 96, period: 64)
//   DeformTable_Shimmer      deform_sine(amplitude: 8,  period: 32)
//   DeformTable_Haze         deform_sine(amplitude: 16, period: 64)
//   DeformTable_Rocking      deform_sine(amplitude: 20, period: 64)
//   DeformTable_Perspective  v_column_floor(center: 20, max_offset: 24)
//
// Declared in configs.emp's own order so a diff against the deleted file reads straight
// across (`git show <pre-P1>:games/sonic4/data/parallax/configs.emp`; the `configs.emp:NNN`
// citations throughout this file and the witness are that file at its final revision).
// The equivalence witness proves each one byte-equal to its generator call independently
// of the records.
// =====================================================================
// THE GENERATOR CALL IS NAMED, AND THE EMITTED `data` INITIALISES FROM THE NAME (Task 7).
// A `pub data` symbol is a LABEL — its bytes are not readable at comptime — so the only
// way the equivalence witness (games/sonic4/test/scene_equiv_proof.emp) can compare the
// emitted tables against the generator calls is if the array VALUE has a name it can
// import. These six consts are that name; scene_registry.emp's `data` lines initialise
// from them, and the emitted bytes are the same call's output either way.
pub const SceneSrc_DeformTable_Zero        = deform_zero()
pub const SceneSrc_DeformTable_OJZ_Calm    = deform_sine(amplitude: 96, period: 64)
pub const SceneSrc_DeformTable_Shimmer     = deform_sine(amplitude: 8,  period: 32)
pub const SceneSrc_DeformTable_Haze        = deform_sine(amplitude: 16, period: 64)
pub const SceneSrc_DeformTable_Rocking     = deform_sine(amplitude: 20, period: 64)
pub const SceneSrc_DeformTable_Perspective = v_column_floor(center: 20, max_offset: 24)
// The seventh, and the first that is not a deform curve: EFFECTS-W1 item 9's ROW REMAP
// LADDER. 17 rows of 16 bytes = 272 B. Row `H - |p|` is selected each frame from the
// perspective quantity and its first `|p|` bytes are consumed. See
// engine/level/parallax_dsl.emp for the three invariants it guarantees by construction, for
// why the model is CHOSEN rather than fitted to S3K's own table, and for why H is 16 and not
// the 64 this started at — the DEBUG shape has only ~558 B of packed-data headroom before the
// bank-placement rule demands a whole-ROM re-layout, measured across two refused builds.
pub const SceneSrc_RowRemapLadder_Waterline16 = row_remap_ladder16()

// =====================================================================
// OJZ_Default — configs.emp:107-114.
//
// Four bands, uniform BG 1/2 depth, whole-plane V-scroll (v_factor_bg 3, v_center 512),
// every band shift 15. The all-zero BG table is kept for byte-identity with the shipped
// header (it USED to be what selected the per-line HScroll pipeline; since 2026-08-26 the
// pipeline is per-line for every scene) while the 15-sentinels skip the (0 >> shift)
// sample loop — flat-pathed. (`precision: PRECISION_LINE` was authored here until the
// field was retired, d-29-corrected.)
//
// THE MASK BRIDGE, USE 1 OF 2. The shipped header declares band_count 4 with
// layer_mask $1F — five bits for four bands. `derived_mask` can only ever produce $0F
// from four enabled layers, so the fifth bit is unreachable from the model and is carried
// as `layer_mask_raw`. scene() checks it is a SUPERSET of the derivation ($1F | $0F ==
// $1F, passes), which is the only thing that can be checked about it.
//
// ---- THE DRIFT, AND WHY IT IS ON ALL FOUR BANDS AT ONE RATE (EFFECTS-W1 item 3) ----
//
// This is the act-installed record (`OJZ_Act1_Descriptor.act_parallax_config`), so it is
// the OJZ background for every section that does not bind an editor scene — 1, 2, 3, 5, 6,
// 7 and 8 of the nine. It is therefore the layer to drift if the drift is to be SEEN.
//
// THE RATE IS THE SAME ON ALL FOUR BANDS, AND THAT IS READ OFF THE ART RATHER THAN CHOSEN
// FOR SYMMETRY. Two facts decide it:
//
//   1. These four bands are ONE VISUAL LAYER. Their fa, fb, dsa and dsb are identical, so
//      today they scroll as one plane and the three band boundaries are invisible. They are
//      four records for the header's sake, not four depths.
//   2. THE BG ART HAS NO BANDS TO ALIGN THEM WITH. Read out of the emitted plane
//      (games/sonic4/data/generated/ojz/act1/zone_bg.bin, 64 x 64 cells): cell rows 0-15
//      repeat VERBATIM at 16, 32 and 48, i.e. one 128-px canopy pattern tiled four times
//      vertically, and its features are VERTICAL — vine columns and flower clusters that run
//      the full height. The band tops are plane cell rows 0 / 8 / 40 / 48, which cut that
//      pattern at no edge it has.
//
// So a per-band rate would shear those vertical features at the band boundary, and the
// boundary is not even stationary: `v_factor: 3` walks the whole plane past the screen as
// the camera climbs the 6144-px act, so the shear line would SWEEP down the picture. One
// rate on all four has no seam by construction — every band's plane-B word gains the same
// pixel offset, so the plane moves as the single sheet it is drawn as.
//
// (A genuinely per-band drift is the right call the moment the BG art HAS bands — a sky
// strip over a treeline over a floor. That is an art decision, not a scene edit, and the
// mechanism is per-band already: change one `Rate(-32)` here and only that band moves.)
//
// THE MAGNITUDE IS -32 = 1/8 px per frame = 7.5 px/s, CORPUS-GROUNDED. It is S3K AIZ1's
// cloud rate exactly ($2000 in AIZ1's own 16.16 accumulator), the slow-ambient value the
// engine's own docs name, and the canopy takes ~43 s to cross the 320-px screen at it —
// visible within a couple of seconds of standing still, and never competing with the
// player's own motion (running Sonic moves this plane ~5 px/frame at FACTOR_1_2, forty
// times the drift). The unit trap is real and worth restating at the call: THE UNIT IS
// 1/256 px PER FRAME, so this is 32/256, not 32 px.
//
// THE SIGN IS NEGATIVE SO THE DRIFT NEVER FIGHTS FORWARD MOTION. Decode_Factor_B returns
// `-decode(camX, factor_b)`, so running RIGHT lowers the plane-B scroll word and the
// background travels LEFT; `add.w (a4), d2` folds the accumulator into that same word, so a
// negative rate lowers it too and the canopy drifts the same way it already moves under a
// player heading right. A positive rate would partially cancel the parallax on the act's
// default direction of travel, which is the artifact you would notice. WHICH WAY THAT IS ON
// SCREEN IS DERIVED HERE, NOT SEEN — SceneDrift's banner says to eyeball it once, and this
// parcel could not. If it reads backwards, the fix is the minus sign on these four lines.
// =====================================================================
pub const Scene_OJZ_Default: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 512,  fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2, dsa: 15, dsb: 15, drift: SceneDrift.Rate(-32)),
              layer(world_y: 1024, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2, dsa: 15, dsb: 15, drift: SceneDrift.Rate(-32)),
              layer(world_y: 3072, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2, dsa: 15, dsb: 15, drift: SceneDrift.Rate(-32)),
              layer(world_y: 3584, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2, dsa: 15, dsb: 15, drift: SceneDrift.Rate(-32)),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer() ],
    count: 4, v_factor: 3, v_center: 512, v_offset: 0,
    deform_bg: SceneDeform.Shared(DeformTable_Zero, 1),
    layer_mask_raw: $1F)

// =====================================================================
// OJZ_Underwater — configs.emp:132-140. THE Parcel W fixture.
//
// The same four layers and factors as OJZ_Default, so anything that differs between the
// two records is the overlay and nothing else. Every authored layer stays at shift 15;
// the world-anchored overlay on patch channel 0 splits whichever layer holds the line and
// forces dsb 2 from there down against the shimmer table.
//
// THE MASK BRIDGE, USE 2 OF 2 — same shape as OJZ_Default (band_count 4, layer_mask $1F).
// These two configs are the complete set of bridge users.
// =====================================================================
pub const Scene_OJZ_Underwater: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 512,  fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2, dsa: 15, dsb: 15),
              // ---- EFFECTS-W1 item 9: THE WATERLINE'S ROW REMAP LANDS ON THIS LAYER ----
              //
              // WHY LAYER 1 AND NOT ANOTHER, MEASURED RATHER THAN REASONED. On the shipped
              // build in OJZ act 1 section 0 (the only section that binds this config and the
              // only one with a live patch channel): Camera_Y 144, Parallax_Current_Vscroll_BG
              // 0, and Effects_Screen_L[0] sweeping 93 -> 75 unattended under the section's
              // `anchor_sweep`. This scene's four tops map to plane lines 0 / 64 / 320 / 384
              // (v_factor 3, v_center 512), so with Vscroll_BG 0 the on-screen bands are
              // 0..63 and 64..223 and the anchor line sits inside the SECOND one. Step 4b
              // splits that band at L and the split inherits the whole record — tail
              // included — so the ladder reaches BOTH halves and the fill's last-wins mark
              // picks the lower one, whose top IS the waterline. That is S3K's own window
              // (HScroll_table+$0DA, the rows below the surface).
              //
              // THE SURFACE PLANE LINE IS 101, AND IT SETS THE EQUILIBRIUM. The perspective
              // quantity is `p = 101 - Vscroll_BG - L`; at the measured rest state that is
              // 101 - 0 - (75..93) = 8..26 lines, so the effect is LIVE and ANIMATING with no
              // player input, because the anchor sweeps.
              //
              // 101 AND NOT 94, AND THE DIFFERENCE WAS MEASURED RATHER THAN TUNED BY EYE. The
              // ladder's compression is QUADRATIC in the line index, so the first few lines of
              // any row are the identity — `entry(r, i) = i + i*i*(H-r)/(H*(H-1))` has a zero
              // quadratic term while i is small. At 94 the sweep ran p = 1..19 and
              // tools/row_remap_witness.py separated the output from the FLAT prediction on
              // only 10 of 12 samples: on the two shortest runs the remap was, truthfully,
              // the identity — design §9.1 precondition 1 arriving through the LADDER rather
              // than through a flat source. 101 puts the whole rest sweep at p >= 8, in the
              // part of the row where the quadratic actually bites.
              //
              // `p == 0` — the equilibrium, where the remap turns itself off with no special
              // case — is now L = 101, about 37 px above the rest position: fly UP through it
              // and the effect thins to nothing and then grows back with the sign inverted.
              // That is the "depending on your perspective" the effect is named for.
              //
              // WHAT VARIES, so the remap is not the identity (design §9.1 precondition 1):
              // this scene's `anchor: SceneAnchor.At(0, 15, 2)` writes dsb 2 into every band
              // from the split down, against DeformTable_Shimmer. That is a +/-2 px per-line
              // wave, and the remap compresses its period toward the far end of the run.
              // THE AMPLITUDE IS THE HONEST WEAK POINT: precondition 1 asks whether the
              // source varies AT ALL, and +/-2 px passes that and is still faint. Turning it
              // up is one number — the anchor's dsb — and it is OWNER CONTENT, not an engine
              // choice, so this parcel changed nothing about the shipped shimmer.
              layer(world_y: 1024, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2, dsa: 15, dsb: 15,
                    rowRemap: SceneRemap.Ladder(RowRemapLadder_Waterline16, 101, 4)),
              layer(world_y: 3072, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2, dsa: 15, dsb: 15),
              layer(world_y: 3584, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2, dsa: 15, dsb: 15),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer() ],
    count: 4, v_factor: 3, v_center: 512, v_offset: 0,
    deform_bg: SceneDeform.Shared(DeformTable_Shimmer, 3),
    anchor: SceneAnchor.At(0, 15, 2),
    layer_mask_raw: $1F)

// =====================================================================
// Scene_VSplitWitness — P3 TASK 11's ACCEPTANCE PROOF, and NOT CONTENT.
//
// It is not in the registry, nothing installs it, and it must not acquire a section binding:
// adopting visible vertical depth on a shipped OJZ scene is owner territory (the Parcel D
// content pass), and this parcel's surface is the MECHANISM. What this scene exists to do is
// make the mechanism falsifiable — it is the scene whose lowering, in
// data/effects/ojz_effects.emp, is compared WORD FOR WORD against the hand-authored
// `OJZ_VSRAM_HAND` program that has been in the tree since Parcel C1. The two must be
// identical, because the lowering is supposed to add no encoder of its own: it calls the same
// `fx_vscroll_split` the hand site calls. A divergence at any word means a second mechanism
// grew, which is the one thing Task 11 is forbidden to do.
//
// WHY IT REPRODUCES THAT PARTICULAR PROGRAM. `OJZ_TestVsram` is the shipped VSRAM fixture:
// one fire, screen line 112, Plane-B scroll $0043, and the program whose LANDING was measured
// at N+1 on the emulator (docs/benchmarks/effects-p3/GATE-EVIDENCE.md — first differing pixel
// row exactly 112). Re-expressing it means the landing evidence carries over by byte identity
// rather than by analogy, which is why the witness's top is 112 and its offset $0043 and not
// two numbers chosen for their own sake. If either fixture constant ever moves, the pins in
// ojz_effects.emp fail loudly and this scene is what gets re-tuned.
//
// THE SHAPE IS THE MINIMUM THAT IS ALSO WELL-FORMED. Two layers, because band 0's top must be
// 0 (Step 4a's search requires ascending tops starting at the plane origin) and the split
// belongs to the SECOND layer's top — the same regional split SkyHaze authors at 112. Locked
// plane (v_factor 15) and v_offset 0, because those are the scenes the two-writer ruling
// leaves legal, and under them scene_vsplit_line() is the identity: authored top 112 IS
// screen line 112.
//
// ZERO BYTES. A Scene is comptime-only; this const emits nothing, in any shape.
// =====================================================================
pub const Scene_VSplitWitness: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0,   fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_4, dsa: 15, dsb: 15),
              layer(world_y: 112, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_4, dsa: 15, dsb: 15,
                    vsplit: SceneVSplit.At($0043)),
              no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer() ],
    count: 2, v_factor: 15, v_center: 0, v_offset: 0)

// =====================================================================
// OJZ_Windy — configs.emp:150-154. One layer, whole plane B at full sine amplitude.
// BG factor 1/4 matches SkyHaze so a Sec0<->Sec1 transition lerps only the deform
// amplitude. layer_mask $01 DERIVES from the single enabled layer — no bridge.
// =====================================================================
pub const Scene_OJZ_Windy: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_4, dsa: 4, dsb: 0),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer() ],
    count: 1, v_factor: 15, v_center: 0, v_offset: 0,
    deform_bg: SceneDeform.Shared(DeformTable_OJZ_Calm, 1))

// =====================================================================
// Shimmer — configs.emp:163-172. Mirrors `shimmer_bg(speed, shift = 2, fg = FACTOR_1,
// bg = FACTOR_1_4)`; all three shipped call sites take the three defaults and vary only
// the speed, so the helper here carries the defaults as literals rather than re-exposing
// parameters no config uses.
// =====================================================================
pub comptime fn shimmer_scene(speed: int) -> Scene {
    return scene(
        layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_4, dsa: 2, dsb: 2),
                  no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
                  no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer() ],
        count: 1, v_factor: 15, v_center: 0, v_offset: 0,
        deform_bg: SceneDeform.Shared(DeformTable_Shimmer, speed))
}
pub const Scene_Shimmer_Slow: Scene = shimmer_scene(speed: 1)   // configs.emp:170
pub const Scene_Shimmer:      Scene = shimmer_scene(speed: 3)   // configs.emp:171 (default)
pub const Scene_Shimmer_Fast: Scene = shimmer_scene(speed: 6)   // configs.emp:172

// =====================================================================
// Haze — configs.emp:181-203. FG heat wobble over the five-band BG gradient.
//
// `gradient: 1` skips the sky/mountain layers (dsa 15) and ramps the near ones (4 then
// 3); `gradient: 0` puts every layer at dsa 3. dsb is 4 on every layer in BOTH arms —
// which is why scene_caps()' live-amplitude scan is cross-plane: the table is attached to
// the FG only, and a scan pairing dsb with deform_bg would fold Haze to no-deform.
//
// The two arms differ in exactly four of the five authored dsa shifts, so they are carried
// as four single-level `if` bindings rather than two whole layer arrays. Flat `let`-level
// ifs only: an `if` in BLOCK-TAIL position evaluates to unit silently.
//
// THE BINDINGS ARE NAMED `dsa0..dsa3`, NOT `d0..d3`, AND THAT IS NOT COSMETIC. `d0`-`d7`
// and `a0`-`a7` are REGISTER tokens in .emp, so `dsa: d0` passes a register where an int
// is wanted. It fails loud (`a register is not a valid int argument — only a Reg parameter
// accepts a register`), but the diagnostic points at the CALL, not at the `let`, so the
// cause is not obvious from the message. Never bind a comptime local to a register name.
// =====================================================================
pub comptime fn haze_scene(speed: int, gradient: int) -> Scene {
    // gradient arm: 15 / 15 / 15 / 4 / 3 — uniform arm: 3 / 3 / 3 / 3 / 3.
    let dsa0 = if gradient == 1 { 15 } else { 3 }
    let dsa1 = if gradient == 1 { 15 } else { 3 }
    let dsa2 = if gradient == 1 { 15 } else { 3 }
    let dsa3 = if gradient == 1 { 4 }  else { 3 }
    return scene(
        layers: [ layer(world_y: 0,   fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_8, dsa: dsa0, dsb: 4),  // clouds
                  layer(world_y: 32,  fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_4, dsa: dsa1, dsb: 4),  // far mtns
                  layer(world_y: 80,  fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_3_8, dsa: dsa2, dsb: 4),  // mid mtns
                  layer(world_y: 112, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2, dsa: dsa3, dsb: 4),  // hills
                  layer(world_y: 160, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1,   dsa: 3,  dsb: 4),  // ground
                  no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer() ],
        count: 5, v_factor: 15, v_center: 0, v_offset: 0,
        deform_fg: SceneDeform.Shared(DeformTable_Haze, speed))
}
pub const Scene_Haze_Slow:    Scene = haze_scene(speed: 1, gradient: 1)   // configs.emp:200
pub const Scene_Haze:         Scene = haze_scene(speed: 2, gradient: 1)   // configs.emp:201
pub const Scene_Haze_Fast:    Scene = haze_scene(speed: 4, gradient: 1)   // configs.emp:202
pub const Scene_Haze_Uniform: Scene = haze_scene(speed: 2, gradient: 0)   // configs.emp:203

// =====================================================================
// Rocking — configs.emp:213-223. Plane B rocks via per-column V-scroll off a sine table;
// BG H-scroll locked (FACTOR_0) to dodge the leftmost-partial-column VDP artifact ON
// PLANE B ONLY — the foreground still scrolls (fa: FACTOR_1) and still shows the sliver;
// see the left-column policy note below — and the all-zero BG H-table forces the per-line
// pipeline.
//
// All three shipped call sites take `shift`'s default 0, so the amplitude shift rides the
// SceneVDeform payload (Columns' third slot) — NOT the v_deform_shift_raw bridge. The
// bridge exists only for SkyHaze, which sets the shift while attaching no table.
// Rocking_Slow's v_speed 0 is a STATIC tilt, not "no V-deform": the table is attached,
// so CAP_PER_COL_VSRAM is raised.
//
// LEFT-COLUMN POLICY: Accept — AND SINCE 2026-08-29 THAT MEANS ACCEPT THE RESIDUAL, NOT
// SHIP THE ARTIFACT. The foreground strip this note described is FIXED: the engine's
// column-19 borrow (Parallax_Step5_Vscroll) puts plane A's V-scroll into column-pair 19's
// plane-B word, so this scene's leading sliver renders the foreground's own scroll on
// every camera position. What Accept now records is the borrow's price — plane B's
// rightmost 16 px carry plane A's V-scroll, and with `v_factor: 15` below that is a
// displacement of camY mod 512, a background seam. Owner ruling d-40; derivation in
// docs/research/2026-08-29-vsram-column19-borrow.md.
//
// The per-plane reading that got us here stands and is worth keeping: fb is FACTOR_0 and
// the sole plane-B H-deform source is DeformTable_Zero (every sample 0), so plane-B
// HScroll is identically zero — TRUE, AND ONLY ABOUT PLANE B. Plane A here is
// `fa: FACTOR_1` (HScroll = -camX, off the 16-px grain at fifteen camera positions in
// sixteen) with `dsa: 4` over the FG table, which is why the FOREGROUND was the plane
// losing its leading sliver (docs/research/2026-08-28-deform-scene-left-edge-triage.md).
//
// TWO INDEPENDENT REASONS FACTOR0LOCK IS UNAVAILABLE HERE: (1) scene()'s Factor0Lock
// cannot see table CONTENTS (a table is a Label at comptime), so a live dsb (4, here)
// against the zero table is indistinguishable from a live one against a real table;
// (2) plane A is not locked at all, and since 2026-08-28 the guard checks that too.
// Re-authoring dsb: 15 would clear reason (1) and NOT reason (2), so it still would not
// buy the Factor0Lock spelling — and since the borrow, Factor0Lock would not buy this
// scene anything anyway: the repair is unconditional and so is its price.
// =====================================================================
pub comptime fn rocking_scene(speed: int, shift: int) -> Scene {
    return scene(
        layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_0, dsa: 4, dsb: 4),
                  no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
                  no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer(),
                  no_layer() ],
        count: 1, v_factor: 15, v_center: 0, v_offset: 0,
        deform_bg: SceneDeform.Shared(DeformTable_Zero, 1),
        v_deform: SceneVDeform.Columns(DeformTable_Rocking, speed, shift),
        left_column_mask: SceneLeftColMask.Accept)
}
pub const Scene_Rocking_Slow: Scene = rocking_scene(speed: 0, shift: 0)   // configs.emp:221 static tilt
pub const Scene_Rocking:      Scene = rocking_scene(speed: 1, shift: 0)   // configs.emp:222
pub const Scene_Rocking_Fast: Scene = rocking_scene(speed: 3, shift: 0)   // configs.emp:223 stormy

// =====================================================================
// Perspective — configs.emp:232-246. V-column floor curve plus a per-layer BG H-shimmer
// that skips sky/mountains (dsb 15), goes faint on the hills (4) and strong on the
// ground (2). Every layer's PLANE-B factor is H-locked (FACTOR_0) for the same VDP quirk
// as Rocking; every layer's plane A is `fa: FACTOR_1` with dsa 4, i.e. not locked at all.
//
// LEFT-COLUMN POLICY (P3 Task 12): Accept — and unlike Rocking's, this Accept was ALWAYS
// a REAL artifact decision rather than a comptime-visibility concession. FACTOR_0 locks
// the BASE plane-B factor, but the Shimmer table is live on plane B for the hills and
// ground layers (dsb 4 / 2), and deform adds per-line plane-B HScroll on top of the lock
// — so on those rows the leftmost partial column exists for most shimmer phases and
// renders at a V-scroll the column buffer never wrote. That is what this family has
// ALWAYS shipped (the "H-locked for the VDP quirk" note above was only ever true of the
// plane-B sky rows); Task 12 makes the decision spelled instead of implied. The Gynoug
// answer. AND THE PLANE-A HALF IS LOUDER THAN THE SHIMMER: `fa: FACTOR_1` on every layer
// means the foreground's own leftmost 16 px go too, on every row and at fifteen camera
// positions in sixteen — the strip reported on scenes 13-15
// (docs/research/2026-08-28-deform-scene-left-edge-triage.md). If the sliver matters
// visually, it is now FIXED rather than masked: the engine's column-19 borrow makes the
// leading sliver render the foreground's own V-scroll (owner ruling d-40; the sprite bar
// was rejected). Accept here therefore records the borrow's price — 16 px of plane B, split
// between the right edge and, on the shimmer rows where plane-B HScroll leaves the grain,
// plane B's own leading sliver. Factor0Lock is out of reach twice over — while the floor
// shimmers, and while the foreground scrolls — by design.
//
// AND ON TWO OF THE THREE THAT PRICE IS NOW DECLINED (d-50, 2026-09-02). This is the family
// whose price the owner actually saw. Plane B is locked (v_factor 15) with
// DeformTable_Shimmer live on the hills and ground rows, so the 16 px the borrow costs
// plane B is not a static seam but a strip drawn from 154-395 px away and re-cut 5-12 times
// a frame — "animating differently and super fast". He ruled the borrow per scene and
// turned it off on the two he was looking at: registry indices 13 (Subtle) and 14
// (Perspective), which is what `left_col: LCM_DECLINE_BORROW` says below.
//
// DRAMATIC IS DELIBERATELY LEFT ON, and that is a decision rather than an oversight: the
// ruling names 13 and 14 and nothing else, and the point of a per-scene switch is that the
// answer is per scene. It is also the cheapest A/B this family will ever offer — three
// instances of one constructor, two declining and one not — if the look needs revisiting.
// One word changes it.
//
// WHAT DECLINING BUYS AND COSTS HERE, so it is not re-derived from the engine banner: plane
// B's leading and trailing 16 px go back to plane B's own V-scroll (correct, and no longer
// re-cut every frame), and plane A's leading `hscroll & 15` sliver goes back to rendering
// the AND of camY with plane B's word — the pre-d-40 foreground strip, on a family whose
// every layer is `fa: FACTOR_1`. Both edges cannot be right at once: the hardware ANDs one
// pair of words and hands the result to both planes.
// =====================================================================
// THE FIVE LAYERS ARE FACTORED OUT so the two constructors below cannot drift apart on the
// half of the scene that is NOT the policy. Sharing them is the whole reason this helper
// exists — the alternative was one constructor taking the policy as a parameter, and that
// is refused by the assembler (see the note on the pair below).
pub comptime fn perspective_layers() -> [SceneLayer; 16] {
    return [ layer(world_y: 0,   fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_0, dsa: 4, dsb: 15),
             layer(world_y: 32,  fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_0, dsa: 4, dsb: 15),
             layer(world_y: 80,  fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_0, dsa: 4, dsb: 15),
             layer(world_y: 112, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_0, dsa: 4, dsb: 4),
             layer(world_y: 160, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_0, dsa: 4, dsb: 2),
             no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
             no_layer(),
             no_layer(),
             no_layer(),
             no_layer(),
             no_layer(),
             no_layer(),
             no_layer(),
             no_layer() ]
}

// TWO CONSTRUCTORS, ONE PER POLICY, AND THE POLICY IS SPELLED IN THE `scene()` CALL. The
// obvious shape — one constructor taking `left_col: SceneLeftColMask` — was built first and
// REFUSED BY SIGIL: a `Type.Variant` path written as an argument to a parameter whose enum
// type was imported from another module resolves as a LABEL, and the build fails with "a
// label is not a valid SceneLeftColMask argument — only a Label parameter accepts a label".
// The same path is fine as an argument to `scene()` or `scene_lcm_is_decline_borrow()`,
// which are declared in the enum's own module, and a named `use ...{SceneLeftColMask}` on
// top of the glob does not help (tried, still red). Binding each arm to a const first DOES
// work and was the first fix here; it was BACKED OUT for a reason worth stating, because
// the workaround was cheaper than what it cost:
//
//   `tools/effects_budget_check.py`'s axis-5 census counts declaration sites by matching
//   `left_column_mask: SceneLeftColMask.<Variant>` in the authored scene modules. Route the
//   policy through a parameter and this family's declaration disappears from that census —
//   the SpriteMask-adopter count stops seeing a whole per-column family. A drift lane that
//   silently stops looking at a scene is worse than a duplicated `scene()` tail.
//
// So the duplication is bought deliberately: five lines twice, with the LAYERS shared above
// so the part that could drift meaningfully cannot. The part that is duplicated is pinned
// anyway — games/sonic4/test/scene_equiv_proof.emp carries an independent field-by-field
// oracle for all THREE Perspective records, so a divergence between these two bodies fails
// the build with the differing field named.

// PERSPECTIVE, BORROW KEPT — the pre-d-50 behaviour and the family's original constructor.
pub comptime fn perspective_scene(v_shift: int, h_speed: int, v_speed: int) -> Scene {
    return scene(
        layers: perspective_layers(),
        count: 5, v_factor: 15, v_center: 0, v_offset: 0,
        deform_bg: SceneDeform.Shared(DeformTable_Shimmer, h_speed),
        v_deform: SceneVDeform.Columns(DeformTable_Perspective, v_speed, v_shift),
        left_column_mask: SceneLeftColMask.Accept)
}

// PERSPECTIVE, BORROW DECLINED — d-50, and the only difference from the constructor above
// is the last argument. Plane B keeps both its edges; plane A's leading sliver goes back to
// the pre-d-40 artifact. See the family banner for why that is the better trade here.
pub comptime fn perspective_scene_declined(v_shift: int, h_speed: int, v_speed: int) -> Scene {
    return scene(
        layers: perspective_layers(),
        count: 5, v_factor: 15, v_center: 0, v_offset: 0,
        deform_bg: SceneDeform.Shared(DeformTable_Shimmer, h_speed),
        v_deform: SceneVDeform.Columns(DeformTable_Perspective, v_speed, v_shift),
        left_column_mask: SceneLeftColMask.DeclineBorrow)
}

// THE POLICY IS PER INSTANCE, NOT PER FAMILY. The ruling names two scenes, not the family
// (d-50: "the shimmer scenes he saw (13 and 14)"), so Dramatic keeps the borrow and each
// call site below names the constructor that carries its own answer.
pub const Scene_Perspective_Subtle:   Scene = perspective_scene_declined(v_shift: 2, h_speed: 1, v_speed: 0)  // :244  registry 13
pub const Scene_Perspective:          Scene = perspective_scene_declined(v_shift: 0, h_speed: 2, v_speed: 1)  // :245  registry 14
pub const Scene_Perspective_Dramatic: Scene = perspective_scene(v_shift: 0, h_speed: 3, v_speed: 2)           // :246  registry 15

// =====================================================================
// WindyHaze — configs.emp:253-262. Composite: a windy multi-band BG gradient (clouds get
// the full wave at dsb 0, the ground none at 15) with a per-layer phase desync, under a
// uniform FG haze at dsa 3. TWO tables, one per plane — the only pair in the set besides
// SkyHaze. The phase column (0/64/128/192/0) is authored per layer.
// =====================================================================
pub const Scene_WindyHaze: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0,   fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_8, dsa: 3, dsb: 0,  phase: 0),
              layer(world_y: 32,  fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_4, dsa: 3, dsb: 1,  phase: 64),
              layer(world_y: 80,  fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_3_8, dsa: 3, dsb: 2,  phase: 128),
              layer(world_y: 112, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2, dsa: 3, dsb: 3,  phase: 192),
              layer(world_y: 160, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1,   dsa: 3, dsb: 15, phase: 0),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer() ],
    count: 5, v_factor: 15, v_center: 0, v_offset: 0,
    deform_fg: SceneDeform.Shared(DeformTable_Haze, 2),
    deform_bg: SceneDeform.Shared(DeformTable_OJZ_Calm, 1))

// =====================================================================
// SkyHaze — configs.emp:269-275. A REGIONAL split at world-Y 112, not a gradient: the top
// layer takes the windy BG with a steady FG, the bottom layer the reverse.
//
// THE V-DEFORM SHIFT BRIDGE, ITS ONE AND ONLY USE. The shipped header passes
// `v_deform_shift_bg: 0` while attaching NO v-deform table, and SceneVDeform.None lowers
// to hdr()'s default 4 — a different byte. `v_deform_shift_raw: 0` reproduces it. The
// value is inert at runtime (no table means the column sampler never runs), which is
// exactly why it is a byte-identity bridge and not model.
// =====================================================================
pub const Scene_SkyHaze: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0,   fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_4, dsa: 15, dsb: 2),
              layer(world_y: 112, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_4, dsa: 2,  dsb: 15),
              no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer() ],
    count: 2, v_factor: 15, v_center: 0, v_offset: 0,
    deform_fg: SceneDeform.Shared(DeformTable_Haze, 2),
    deform_bg: SceneDeform.Shared(DeformTable_OJZ_Calm, 1),
    v_deform_shift_raw: 0)

// =====================================================================
// OJZ_Caves — configs.emp:283-291. Slow BG parallax (the far layers barely move at
// FACTOR_1_16) with the section-transition flag set. Same five-layer shape as the
// LockedClouds scene; only the B-plane factors differ. All-zero flat-pathed H-deform, and
// layer_mask $1F DERIVES from five enabled layers.
// =====================================================================
pub const Scene_OJZ_Caves: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0,   fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_16, dsa: 15, dsb: 15),
              layer(world_y: 32,  fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_16, dsa: 15, dsb: 15),
              layer(world_y: 80,  fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_8,  dsa: 15, dsb: 15),
              layer(world_y: 112, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_4,  dsa: 15, dsb: 15),
              layer(world_y: 160, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1,    dsa: 15, dsb: 15),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer() ],
    count: 5, v_factor: 15, v_center: 0, v_offset: 0,
    transition: TRANS_INSTANT,
    deform_bg: SceneDeform.Shared(DeformTable_Zero, 1))

// =====================================================================
// OJZ_LockedClouds — configs.emp:299-307. The shipped header's layer_mask $1E clears
// bit 0, so the cloud band falls through the band-inheritance path and scrolls locked
// while the rest of plane B parallaxes.
//
// THIS IS THE NEAR MISS, AND IT IS NOT A BRIDGE. $1E DERIVES — from `enabled: 0` on
// layer 0 of five real layers — and the derived path was byte-verified. Authoring it as
// `layer_mask_raw: $1E` would type-check and produce the same byte while hiding the one
// fact this config exists to express, and would surrender the superset guard for nothing.
// The layer stays REAL (inside count: 5, so it is still lowered as band 0 with its own
// factors); only its mask bit is clear.
// =====================================================================
pub const Scene_OJZ_LockedClouds: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0,   fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_8, dsa: 15, dsb: 15, enabled: 0),
              layer(world_y: 32,  fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_4, dsa: 15, dsb: 15),
              layer(world_y: 80,  fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_3_8, dsa: 15, dsb: 15),
              layer(world_y: 112, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2, dsa: 15, dsb: 15),
              layer(world_y: 160, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1,   dsa: 15, dsb: 15),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer() ],
    count: 5, v_factor: 15, v_center: 0, v_offset: 0,
    transition: TRANS_INSTANT,
    deform_bg: SceneDeform.Shared(DeformTable_Zero, 1))
